{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is running a cobbler-scaffold stitch task (#5420) that requires implementing `cmd/shuf` for the go-unix-utils project. Specifically, the task requires implementing only requirements R1.1-R1.4 from srd064-shuf.yaml, which cover the **default shuffle behavior** of the GNU `shuf` command. The deliverables are two files: `cmd/shuf/main.go` (implementation) and `cmd/shuf/shuf_test.go` (differential tests against `gshuf`). The acceptance criteria require: successful compilation, passing `go vet`, passing `go test` (or graceful skip if gshuf not in PATH), and all four R1.x requirements exercised by tests.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - GNU `shuf` command reimplementation in Go (subset: R1.1-R1.4 only)\n   - Random line permutation from files or stdin\n   - Differential testing against Homebrew reference binary `gshuf`\n   - Non-deterministic output testing (structural property verification, not byte equality)\n   - SIGPIPE handler installation via `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests`, `BuildBinary`, `DiffTest` patterns\n   - Graceful skip when reference binary not found (`exec.LookPath`)\n   - Go module: `github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils`\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd064-shuf.yaml** (read in full)\n     - This is the SRD defining all shuf requirements. Only R1.1-R1.4 are in scope.\n     - R1.1: Read all lines from FILE arguments, randomly permute, write to stdout\n     - R1.2: Read from stdin when no files given or \"-\" is filename  \n     - R1.3: Output each input line exactly once in random order (permutation, not sampling with replacement) unless -r is given\n     - R1.4: Treat each line as newline-terminated; last line without newline must be included\n     - Non-goals: No specific PRNG algorithm guarantee, no --random-source compatibility testing\n   \n   - **pkg/sys/sigpipe.go** (provided in project_context)\n     - Contains `InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` - must be called at start of main()\n   \n   - **pkg/testutils/difftest.go** (provided in project_context)\n     - Contains `DiffTest` struct, `RunDiffTests`, `BuildBinary`, `NormalizeFunc`, `ComposeNormalizers`\n     - Key: DiffTest has fields: Name, Args, Stdin, Env, WorkDir, ExitCode, Normalize, ExpectedFiles\n   \n   - **pkg/testutils/build.go** (provided in project_context)\n     - Contains `BuildBinary(t, \".\")` for compiling the cmd package\n   \n   - **cmd/shuf/main.go** - TO BE CREATED\n   - **cmd/shuf/shuf_test.go** - TO BE CREATED\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet. No code has been written.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Read the SRD to understand requirements R1.1-R1.4\n   - Key challenge: differential tests for shuf must verify **structural properties** (correct line count, all input lines present, no duplicates) rather than exact byte equality, since output is randomly ordered\n   - Scope is strictly R1.1-R1.4 (basic shuffle from files/stdin). Flags like -i, -n, -r, -e, -z, -o are NOT in scope for this task (they belong to R2 and R3)\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - The initial massive task prompt containing: role definition, repository file listing, project context (vision, architecture, specifications, roadmap, analysis, source code, requirement states), task description, execution constitution, go style constitution, constraints, shared protocols, package contracts, and the specific task details for implementing cmd/shuf R1.1-R1.4\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Create `cmd/shuf/main.go` implementing R1.1-R1.4 (read lines from files/stdin, randomly permute, write to stdout)\n   - Create `cmd/shuf/shuf_test.go` with differential tests against gshuf\n   - Run `go build -o bin/shuf ./cmd/s